{"content":[{"id":"3076a266","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"42cec704","settings":{"__dynamic__":{"image":"[elementor-tag id=\"\" name=\"post-featured-image\" settings=\"%7B%22fallback%22%3A%7B%22url%22%3A%22%22%2C%22id%22%3A%22%22%2C%22size%22%3A%22%22%7D%7D\"]"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"theme-post-featured-image","elType":"widget"},{"id":"382f39b6","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/expert-plumbing-services-in-springfield-hendersonville-white-house-and-beyond\/\"><b>plumbing problems<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> don\u2019t start as emergencies. They build slowly over time, showing small warning signs before turning into leaks, water damage, or costly repairs.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The challenge is knowing when a problem is something you can handle and when it\u2019s time to call a professional.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At Petitt Heating &amp; Cooling, we help homeowners across Springfield, Hendersonville, White House, and surrounding Middle Tennessee communities catch plumbing issues early before they turn into bigger problems.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you\u2019re noticing something off with your plumbing, here are the key signs it\u2019s time to call a plumber.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"378c41c5","settings":{"title":"Quick Answer: When Should You Call a Plumber?\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"69659eed","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You should call a plumber when you notice recurring leaks, low water pressure, slow or backed-up drains, unusual noises, water damage, or plumbing issues that keep coming back. These signs often indicate deeper problems that require professional repair.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6000b3b6","settings":{"title":"1. Recurring Leaks That Keep Coming Back\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"42d6a894","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A single drip might not seem like a big deal, but leaks that keep returning are usually a sign of a larger issue.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common causes include:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Worn-out fittings or seals<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pipe corrosion<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water pressure problems<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4e743e3e","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Temporary fixes only go so far. If leaks continue to return, it\u2019s a sign you need <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/plumbing\/pipe-and-leak-repair\/\"><b>pipe and leak repair<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> before the problem gets worse.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"75ff0ca8","settings":{"title":"2. Low Water Pressure Throughout Your Home"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"33bd92fb","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your water pressure suddenly drops, it\u2019s often more than just an inconvenience.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Possible causes:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Hidden leaks<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pipe blockages<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mineral buildup<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Issues with the main water line<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"67d03e05","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If multiple fixtures are affected, it often means the problem goes beyond a single fixture and needs a closer look.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4322b409","settings":{"title":"3. Slow or Frequently Backed-Up Drains"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"413459d4","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A slow drain is often the first warning sign of a developing clog.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Watch for:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water draining slowly<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Gurgling sounds<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Frequent clogs in the same drain<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1d144e5b","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If the problem keeps coming back, it may indicate a deeper blockage or even a <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/plumbing\/sewer-services\/\"><b>sewer line issue<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">.<\/span><\/a><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3112ce0a","settings":{"title":"4. Unusual Noises in Your Pipes"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3c77f833","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your plumbing system shouldn\u2019t make loud or unusual noises.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Common warning sounds:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Banging or knocking (water hammer)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Gurgling (drain or vent issues)<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Whistling (pressure problems)<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"21c9895","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These sounds often point to pressure imbalances or airflow issues that need professional attention.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1edd094f","settings":{"title":"5. Water Stains, Moisture, or Mold\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7b797729","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Visible signs of water damage should never be ignored.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Look for:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water stains on ceilings or walls<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Damp spots under sinks<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Musty odors<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.epa.gov\/mold\/brief-guide-mold-moisture-and-your-home\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mold growth<\/span><\/a><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"23a8476d","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These issues often indicate hidden leaks that can lead to structural damage if left untreated.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1c805c68","settings":{"title":"6. Sudden Increase in Your Water Bill"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"54e72321","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If your water bill spikes without a clear reason, there\u2019s likely a hidden issue.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This could be caused by:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Undetected leaks<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Running toilets<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Underground pipe problems<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6fe9cac5","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Even small leaks can waste a significant amount of water over time.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"352141c0","settings":{"title":"7. Multiple Plumbing Issues at Once\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"39daef36","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you\u2019re experiencing more than one issue at the same time, it\u2019s often a sign of a larger system problem.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For example:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Low pressure + slow drains<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Backups in multiple fixtures<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Leaks + rising water bills<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"49103e58","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At that point, it\u2019s less about a single fix and more about finding and addressing the root cause before it leads to bigger damage.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"70d64179","settings":{"title":"Why Small Plumbing Problems Turn Into Big Repairs\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"b13e556","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plumbing systems are connected, which means one issue can affect multiple parts of your home.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">What starts as:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A slow leak<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A minor clog<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A small pressure issue<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"2431d8fb","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">can turn into:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water damage<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pipe failure<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sewer backups<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Expensive repairs<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4704fbfb","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The earlier you address the problem, the more options you have.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"57f42e3f","settings":{"title":"What You Can Handle vs When to Call a Plumber"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3fca3754","settings":{"title":"Safe DIY Fixes:","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"385a3e01","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Replacing air filters in fixtures<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Clearing minor clogs<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Tightening loose fittings<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Checking visible connections<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7d717242","settings":{"title":"Call a Professional If:\n","header_size":"h3","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=secondary"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"19066045","settings":{"editor":"<ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The issue keeps returning<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can\u2019t find the source<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Multiple fixtures are affected<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There are signs of <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.consumerreports.org\/home-garden\/home-maintenance-repairs\/signs-of-water-damage-in-your-home-a1106287412\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">water damage<\/span><\/a><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You suspect a leak behind walls or underground<\/span><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1a8c1c64","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you\u2019re unsure, it\u2019s always better to have it checked early.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"39448f0","settings":{"title":"How Petitt Heating & Cooling Helps"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"453a9aa2","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">At Petitt Heating &amp; Cooling, we help homeowners stay ahead of plumbing problems with reliable service and clear recommendations.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We provide:<\/span><\/p><ul><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Leak detection and repair<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drain cleaning and clog removal<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Water pressure diagnostics<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Sewer line inspections<\/span><\/li><li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/spring-plumbing-maintenance-checklist\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Preventive plumbing maintenance<\/span><\/a><\/li><\/ul>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1bb5582","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our focus is on identifying the real cause of the problem and fixing it the right way.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3f16e40b","settings":{"title":"Plumbing Warning Signs FAQs\n\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"17a15d56","settings":{"items":[{"item_title":"What is considered a plumbing emergency?","_id":"b1f25e5"},{"item_title":"Can I ignore a small plumbing leak?","_id":"1f42309"},{"item_title":"Why do my drains keep clogging?","_id":"e9a76d0"},{"_id":"eeb3b14","item_title":"Is low water pressure always a plumbing issue?"},{"_id":"913e57c","item_title":"How do plumbers find hidden leaks?"}],"__globals__":{"title_typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=accent"}},"elements":[{"id":"97ce4bf","settings":{"_title":"item #1","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"4788e507","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A plumbing emergency includes burst pipes, major leaks, sewer backups, or anything causing active water damage. These issues require immediate professional attention.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"d4f57ec","settings":{"_title":"item #2","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"14a0e780","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">No. Small leaks often get worse over time and can lead to water damage, mold, and higher repair costs.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"1254a7f8","settings":{"_title":"item #3","content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"39712321","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Recurring clogs are usually caused by buildup, pipe damage, or sewer line issues. If it keeps happening, a deeper inspection is needed.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"b9aec9f","settings":{"_title":"Item #4"},"elements":[{"id":"742ba089","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Not always, but sudden or widespread pressure loss often indicates a leak, blockage, or system problem.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true},{"id":"45ac879d","settings":{"_title":"Item #5"},"elements":[{"id":"4bdc2f03","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Plumbers use specialized tools like pressure testing, moisture detection, and camera inspections to locate leaks without damaging your home.<\/span><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container","isLocked":true}],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"nested-accordion","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6e5c6ffe","settings":{"title":"Don\u2019t Wait Until It Becomes an Emergency\n"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"4191312f","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Most major plumbing problems start with small warning signs.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Recognizing those signs early gives you more time, more options, and a better chance of avoiding costly repairs.<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If something doesn\u2019t seem right, it\u2019s worth having it checked.<\/span><\/p><p><b>Call Petitt Heating &amp; Cooling or <\/b><a href=\"https:\/\/petittheatingandcooling.com\/contact-us\/request-an-appointment\/\"><b>schedule service online<\/b><\/a><b> today to keep your plumbing system running smoothly.<\/b><\/p>"},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"}],"settings":{"template":"default"},"metadata":{"ao_post_optimize":"a:6:{s:16:\"ao_post_optimize\";s:2:\"on\";s:19:\"ao_post_js_optimize\";s:2:\"on\";s:20:\"ao_post_css_optimize\";s:2:\"on\";s:12:\"ao_post_ccss\";s:2:\"on\";s:16:\"ao_post_lazyload\";s:2:\"on\";s:15:\"ao_post_preload\";s:0:\"\";}","et_enqueued_post_fonts":"a:3:{s:6:\"family\";a:1:{s:12:\"et-gf-oswald\";s:34:\"Oswald:200,300,regular,500,600,700\";}s:6:\"subset\";a:2:{i:0;s:5:\"latin\";i:1;s:9:\"latin-ext\";}s:9:\"cache_key\";s:73:\"{\"gph\":-1,\"divi\":\"4.27.4\",\"wp\":\"6.9\",\"enable_all_character_sets\":\"false\"}\";}"}}